      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> The <b>router advertisement</b> and discovery evidence show an IPv6 path that the IPv4 pass could not observe. They do not expand our authorization. The report should distinguish the verified finding from the need to confirm future scope across both address families.",
      "taskInstructions": "",
      "taskQuestion": "What is the defensible lesson from the IPv6 finding?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> Correct. Assessment plans should explicitly address both paths for assets that are approved for testing.",
      "answers": [
        "IPv6 addresses should always be treated as out of assessment scope.",
        "IPv6 deployment makes network segmentation unnecessary.",
        "Assessment plans should explicitly check both IPv4 and IPv6 exposure for approved assets.",
        "An IPv4 scan automatically covers all IPv6 exposure too."
